Rust reference
==============
Source: https://github.com/mingtsay/vlmcsd-rs
Revision: 010300220fa2aba848a45ce8073ae3e19869d8de
Upstream declares MIT in its README and workspace manifest.

crates/vlmcsd-protocol/src/aes.rs adapts the upstream vlmcsd-crypto/src/aes.rs, including its
NIST and KMS variant tests. The port removes unsafe native-endian key mutation,
uses fixed-size array chunks, and replaces CBC/MAC buffer handling.
crates/vlmcsd/tests/async_server.rs adapts the request/bind layout and three-version roundtrip
coverage from upstream vlmcsd-network/tests/integration.rs to Tokio, ephemeral
ports, joined task lifetimes, NDR64, and independent Python fixtures.
Copyright remains with mingtsay/vlmcsd-rs contributors and respective authors.
Upstream credits Wind4/vlmcsd and its contributors as its protocol source.

